1
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:03,934
CREAK

2
00:00:04,020 --> 00:00:05,900
Run.

3
00:00:07,180 --> 00:00:10,968
- I'm The Doctor, by the way. What's your name?
- Rose.
- Nice to meet you.

4
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:12,288
Run for your life.

5
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:23,368
It'll follow us!
The hordes of Genghis Khan couldn't get through
that door. Believe me, they tried.

6
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:25,655
Are you alien? Yes.

7
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:32,734
You could come with me.
Is it always this dangerous? Yeah.

8
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:41,171
Right, Rose Tyler, you tell me -

9
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:45,480
where do you wanna go? Backwards
or forwards in time? Your choice.

10
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:47,335
What's it gonna be?

11
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:48,614
Forwards.

12
00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:55,975
How far? ...One hundred years.

13
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:02,778
TARDIS REVS AND GROANS

14
00:01:05,780 --> 00:01:09,932
Step outside those doors - it's
the 22nd century. You're kidding.

15
00:01:10,020 --> 00:01:13,330
That's a bit boring, though.
D'you wanna go further? Fine by me.

16
00:01:20,820 --> 00:01:23,288
Ten thousand years in the future.

17
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:27,532
Step outside - it's the year 12005.
The new Roman Empire.

18
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:31,659
You think you're so impressive.
I am so impressive. You wish!

19
00:01:31,740 --> 00:01:35,528
Right, then. You asked for it.
I know exactly where to go.

20
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:39,850
Hold on!

21
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:42,816
TARDIS GROANS AND ROARS

22
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:52,613
PING!

23
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:55,732
Where are we?

24
00:01:55,820 --> 00:01:57,811
FAINT CREAKS

25
00:01:59,140 --> 00:02:01,290
What's out there?

26
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:33,693
You lot... you spend all your time
thinking about dying.

27
00:02:33,780 --> 00:02:39,571
Like you're gonna get killed
by eggs or beef
or global warming or asteroids.

28
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:44,529
But you never take time to imagine
the impossible,
that maybe you survive.

29
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:50,213
This is the year 5.5/Apple/26.

30
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:52,655
Five billion years in your future.

31
00:02:52,740 --> 00:02:54,890
And this is the day...

32
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:56,857
Hold on...

33
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:05,568
This is the day the sun expands.

34
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:09,654
Welcome to the end of the world.

35
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:01,374
Shuttles five and six now docking.

36
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:03,371
Guests are reminded

37
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:07,897
that Platform One forbids the use of
weapons, teleportation and religion.

38
00:04:09,660 --> 00:04:12,697
Earth-death is scheduled for 15:39,

39
00:04:12,780 --> 00:04:16,295
followed by drinks in the Manchester Suite.

40
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:18,888
So when it says "guests",
does that mean people?

41
00:04:18,980 --> 00:04:22,131
Depends what you mean by people.
I mean people. What do you mean?

42
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:26,896
Aliens. What are they doing on board
this space-ship? What's it all for?

43
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:29,972
It's not really a spaceship,
more like an observation deck.

44
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:34,190
The great and the good are gathering
to watch the planet burn. What for?

45
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:35,419
Fun.

46
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:41,649
Mind you, when I say "the great and
the good" what I mean is the rich.

47
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:46,211
But, hold on, they did this once on
Newsround Extra, the sun expanding,

48
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:48,177
it takes hundreds of years. Millions.

49
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:52,412
But the planet's now the property
of the National Trust.
They've been keeping it preserved.

50
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:56,334
See down there? Gravity satellites
holding back the sun.

51
00:04:56,420 --> 00:05:00,333
The planet looks
the same as ever. I thought
the continents shifted and things.

52
00:05:00,420 --> 00:05:07,132
They did. The Trust moved 'em back.
That's a Classic Earth. Now the
money's run out, nature takes over.

53
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:08,733
How long's it got?

54
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:12,170
About half an hour.
Then the planet gets roasted.

55
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:14,170
Is that why we're here?

56
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:16,171
I mean, is that what you do?

57
00:05:16,260 --> 00:05:18,376
Jump in at the last
minute and save the Earth?

58
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:20,974
I'm not saving it. Time's up.

59
00:05:21,060 --> 00:05:26,540
But what about the people? It's
empty. They've all gone. All left.

60
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:31,289
Just me, then.
Who the hell are you?

61
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:34,531
Oh, that's nice. Thanks(!)
But how did you get in?

62
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:39,648
This is a maximum hospitality zone,
the guests have disembarked. They're
on their way! Any second now...

63
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:45,736
No, that's me, I'm a guest. Look,
I've got an invitation. Look. Y'see?
It's fine. "The Doctor plus one".

64
00:05:45,820 --> 00:05:51,611
I'm the Doctor, this is Rose Tyler,
she's my plus one. That all right?
Well, obviously.

65
00:05:51,700 --> 00:05:53,736
Apologies, et cetera.

66
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:57,960
If you're on board,
we'd better start.

67
00:05:57,180 --> 00:05:58,329
Enjoy.

68
00:06:00,460 --> 00:06:03,896
The paper's slightly psychic. It
shows whatever I want them to see.

69
00:06:03,980 --> 00:06:08,895
Saves a lot of time.
He's blue. Yeah... OK.

70
00:06:08,980 --> 00:06:15,977
We have in attendance the Doctor
and Rose Tyler. Thank you.
All staff to their positions!

71
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:20,656
Hurry now! Thank you! Quick as
we can, come along, come along!

72
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:27,134
And now, might I introduce
the next honoured guest?
Representing the Forest of Cheam

73
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:28,938
we have trees,

74
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:31,693
namely Jabe, Lute and Coffa.

75
00:06:31,780 --> 00:06:38,333
There will be an exchange of gifts
representing peace. If you could keep
the room circulating, thank you...

76
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:44,768
Next, from the solicitors Jolco &
Jolco, we have the Moxx of Balhoon.

77
00:06:44,860 --> 00:06:47,772
And next,
from Financial Family Seven,

78
00:06:47,860 --> 00:06:50,932
we have
the Adherents of the Repeated Meme.

79
00:06:51,020 --> 00:06:56,572
The inventors of hyposlip travel
systems, the brothers Hop Pyleen!

80
00:06:56,660 --> 00:07:02,895
..Cal "Spark" Plug... Mrs and Mrs
Pacoon... The ambassadors from
the City-State of Binding Light...

81
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:08,577
A gift of peace. I bring you
a cutting of my grandfather.

82
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:12,458
Thank you, yes...
Gifts, um...

83
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:15,134
Ahem! I give you in return...

84
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:16,892
air from my lungs.

85
00:07:19,660 --> 00:07:22,572
How... intimate.

86
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:26,573
There's more where that came from.
I bet there is.

87
00:07:26,660 --> 00:07:31,780
..Our friend from
the Silver Devastation, the sponsor
of the main event, please welcome...

88
00:07:31,860 --> 00:07:34,738
..the Face of Boe.

89
00:07:36,820 --> 00:07:39,209
The Moxx of Balhoon.

90
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:42,610
My felicitations
upon this historical happenstance.

91
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:44,611
I bring the gift of bodily salivas.

92
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:47,612
HAWKS AND SPITS
Thank you very much.

93
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:54,816
Ah, the Adherents of the Repeated
Meme! I bring you air from my lungs.

94
00:07:57,460 --> 00:08:00,452
A gift of peace. In all good faith.

95
00:08:00,540 --> 00:08:04,533
..And last but not least,
our very special guest.

96
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:09,455
Ladies and gentlemen
and trees and multiforms,

97
00:08:09,540 --> 00:08:13,499
consider the Earth, below.
In memory of this dying world,

98
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:15,218
we call forth...

99
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:18,531
the Last Human.

100
00:08:18,620 --> 00:08:23,570
The Lady Cassandra O'Brien Dot Delta
Seventeen.

101
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:27,452
Oh, now don't stare! I know,
I know - it's shocking, isn't it?

102
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:34,730
I've had my chin completely taken
away, and look at the difference,
look how thin I am!

103
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:37,493
Thin and dainty!

104
00:08:37,580 --> 00:08:39,730
I don't look a day over 2, 000.

105
00:08:39,820 --> 00:08:42,618
(Moisturise me, moisturise me!)

106
00:08:44,060 --> 00:08:51,978
Truly, I am the Last Human.
My father was a Texan, my
mother was from the Arctic Desert.

107
00:08:52,060 --> 00:08:59,570
They were born on the Earth,
and they were the last to be buried
in its soil.

108
00:08:59,140 --> 00:09:02,610
I have come to honour them...

109
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:05,419
HER VOICE BREAKS
..and say goodbye.

110
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:09,950
Oh, no tears, no tears...

111
00:09:09,180 --> 00:09:10,613
I'm sorry.

112
00:09:12,540 --> 00:09:14,656
But behold!

113
00:09:14,740 --> 00:09:16,571
I bring gifts!

114
00:09:16,660 --> 00:09:21,734
>From Earth itself,
the last remaining ostrich egg.

115
00:09:21,820 --> 00:09:28,134
Legend says
it had a wing-span of 50 feet
and blew fire from its nostrils.

116
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:30,290
Or was that my THIRD husband?

117
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:35,659
Oh, no, oh, don't laugh,
I'll get laughter-lines. No, stop!

118
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:39,699
SHE GIGGLES
Mercy!

119
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:43,489
And here! Another rarity.

120
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:47,812
According to the archives,
this was called an iPod,

121
00:09:47,900 --> 00:09:51,813
it stores classical music from
humanity's greatest composers.

122
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:53,492
Play on!

123
00:09:58,300 --> 00:10:01,736
INTRO TO "Tainted Love" by Soft Cell

124
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:05,889
The refreshments will now be served.

125
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:08,130
Earth-death in 30 minutes.

126
00:10:08,220 --> 00:10:13,692
MARC ALMOND:
# Sometimes I feel I've got to
Run away

127
00:10:13,780 --> 00:10:16,692
# I've got to
Get away... #

128
00:10:16,780 --> 00:10:19,738
POLITE CHAT

129
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:28,178
#... The love we share
Seems to go nowhere

130
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:30,820
# And I've lost my light

131
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:34,609
# For I toss and turn
I can't sleep at night... #

132
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:36,656
Doctor.

133
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:38,219
Thank you.

134
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:43,413
A gift of peace.
In all good faith.

135
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:46,697
Er, no, you're very kind,
but I'm just the steward.

136
00:10:46,780 --> 00:10:49,214
A gift of PEACE.
In all good FAITH.

137
00:10:49,300 --> 00:10:52,133
Oh... yes. Thank you.

138
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:53,414
Of course.

139
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:55,172
Identify species.

140
00:10:57,220 --> 00:11:00,212
Please identify species.
IT WHISTLES

141
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:04,293
Now stop it! Identify his race.
Where's he from?

142
00:11:04,380 --> 00:11:06,848
IT WHISTLES AND TRILLS

143
00:11:07,820 --> 00:11:09,970
It's impossible.

144
00:11:37,260 --> 00:11:39,854
Sorry, am I allowed to be in 'ere?

145
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:44,331
..You have to give us
permission to talk.

146
00:11:44,420 --> 00:11:46,888
Um...

147
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:50,576
Y-You have permission.

148
00:11:50,660 --> 00:11:52,935
Thank you.

149
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:57,332
And, no, you're not in the way.
Guests are allowed anywhere. Oh.

150
00:11:59,740 --> 00:12:01,776
BUTTONS BLEEP

151
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:03,452
What's your name?

152
00:12:03,540 --> 00:12:05,451
Raffalo.

153
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:07,530
Raffalo?

154
00:12:07,140 --> 00:12:08,778
Yes, miss.

155
00:12:08,860 --> 00:12:12,853
I... I won't be long I've just got
to carry out some maintenance.

156
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:16,728
There's a tiny little glitch
in the Face of Boe's suite.

157
00:12:16,820 --> 00:12:23,658
There must be something blocking
the system. He's getting no hot
water. So... you're a plumber?

158
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:25,731
That's right miss.

159
00:12:25,820 --> 00:12:28,500
They still have plumbers?

160
00:12:28,140 --> 00:12:30,529
I hope so, else I'm out of a job!

161
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:34,453
Where are you from? Crespallion.

162
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:38,371
That's a planet, is it?

163
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:44,979
No, Crespallion's part
of the Jaggit Brocade affiliated
to the Scarlet Junction. Convex 56.

164
00:12:45,060 --> 00:12:51,100
And where are you from, miss?
If you don't mind my asking?
No, not at all...

165
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:53,216
Um, I dunno

166
00:12:53,300 --> 00:12:55,768
A long way away.

167
00:12:55,860 --> 00:13:00,172
I just sort of hitched a lift
with this man...

168
00:13:00,260 --> 00:13:04,811
I didn't even think about it.
Don't even know who he is.

169
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:09,495
He's a complete stranger.

170
00:13:11,180 --> 00:13:14,695
Anyway, um, don't let me keep you.
Good luck with it!

171
00:13:14,780 --> 00:13:17,169
Thank you, miss. And, er...

172
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:21,480
thank you for the permission. Not
many people are that considerate.

173
00:13:21,140 --> 00:13:23,938
OK... See you later.

174
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:33,180
Now, then.

175
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:36,920
Control, I'm at junction 19. I think
the problem's coming from in here.

176
00:13:36,180 --> 00:13:38,296
I'll go inside and have a look.

177
00:13:39,380 --> 00:13:42,611
IRREGULAR CLICKS
What's that?
Is there something in there?

178
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:45,612
Ooh, who are you, then?

179
00:13:45,700 --> 00:13:46,655
Hold on!

180
00:13:48,220 --> 00:13:53,169
If you're an upgrade,
I just need to register you,
that's all. Oh, come back.

181
00:13:55,180 --> 00:13:56,659
Ah, there you are.

182
00:13:56,740 --> 00:13:59,379
Now, I just need to register
your ident.

183
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:04,414
Aw, there's two of ya!
Got yourself a little mate?

184
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:06,570
MORE AND MORE CLICKS

185
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:11,176
I think I'd better report this to
control. How many of you ARE there?

186
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:14,971
What are you?

187
00:14:15,060 --> 00:14:16,413
Oh, no!

188
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:18,456
NO! NO-O-O!

189
00:14:28,140 --> 00:14:31,212
MUTED BLEEPS
What's that?

190
00:14:31,300 --> 00:14:34,292
MORE BLEEPS
Well, how should I know?

191
00:14:35,940 --> 00:14:40,580
PING!
Would the owner of the blue box
in Private Gallery 15

192
00:14:40,140 --> 00:14:43,815
please report to
the steward's office immediately.

193
00:14:43,900 --> 00:14:49,418
Guests are reminded that
the use of teleportation
devices is strictly forbidden

194
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:53,778
under peace treaty 5.4/cup/16.
Thank you.

195
00:14:53,860 --> 00:14:58,920
'Earth-death in 25 minutes.

196
00:14:58,180 --> 00:15:00,296
'Earthdeath in 25 minutes.'

197
00:15:00,380 --> 00:15:01,813
Oh, thanks.

198
00:15:08,060 --> 00:15:09,812
Hello!

199
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:11,492
My name's Rose.

200
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:14,219
That's a... sort of plant.

201
00:15:14,300 --> 00:15:15,972
We might be related.

202
00:15:18,060 --> 00:15:19,778
I'm talking to a twig.

203
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:35,808
Oi now, careful with that,
park it properly. No scratches.

204
00:15:37,060 --> 00:15:38,698
ALIEN LANGUAGE

205
00:15:56,860 --> 00:15:59,249
Rose, are you in there?

206
00:16:01,020 --> 00:16:02,578
Aye-aye!

207
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:06,895
What d'you think, then? Great, yeah.

208
00:16:06,980 --> 00:16:12,293
Fine. Once you get past
the slightly psychic paper.

209
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:15,929
They're just so alien!

210
00:16:17,340 --> 00:16:20,252
The aliens are so alien.

211
00:16:21,740 --> 00:16:24,732
You look at 'em...
and they're alien.

212
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:27,380
Good thing I didn't take you
to the deep South(!)

213
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:31,171
Where are you from?

214
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:33,490
All over the place.

215
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:38,973
They all speak English. No,
you just hear English. It's a gift
of the Tardis. Telepathic field,

216
00:16:39,060 --> 00:16:42,211
gets inside your brain, translates.
It's inside MY brain?

217
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:46,373
Well, in a good way.
Your machine gets inside my head?

218
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:51,580
It gets inside and it changes
my mind, and you didn't even ask?
I didn't think about it like that.

219
00:16:51,660 --> 00:16:55,892
No, you were too busy thinking up
cheap shots about the deep South!

220
00:16:55,980 --> 00:17:02,215
Who are YOU, then, Doctor? What're
you called? What sort of alien
are you? I'm just the Doctor.

221
00:17:02,300 --> 00:17:07,135
>From what planet? It's not as if
you'd know it where it is(!) Where
are you from? What's it matter?

222
00:17:07,220 --> 00:17:12,550
Tell me who you are! THIS is who
I am, right here, right now,
all right? All that counts

223
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:16,770
is here and now. And this is me.
Yes, and I'm here too, cos you
brought me here. So just tell me!

224
00:17:25,660 --> 00:17:28,413
'Earth-death in 20 minutes,

225
00:17:30,140 --> 00:17:33,257
'Earth-death in 20 minutes.'

226
00:17:40,340 --> 00:17:43,332
All right.

227
00:17:43,420 --> 00:17:48,778
As my mate Shireen says, don't argue
with the designated driver.

228
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:53,373
Can't exactly call for a taxi.

229
00:17:53,460 --> 00:17:56,293
No signal.

230
00:17:56,380 --> 00:17:59,530
We're out of range. Just a bit.

231
00:18:01,140 --> 00:18:06,658
Tell you what. With a little bit
of jiggery-pokery... Is that a
technical term, jiggery-pokery(?)

232
00:18:06,740 --> 00:18:09,459
Yes, I came first in jiggery-pokery.
What about you?

233
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:11,974
No, failed hullabaloo. Aw.

234
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:15,813
There you go.

235
00:18:22,860 --> 00:18:24,851
PHONE RINGS AT OTHER END

236
00:18:27,460 --> 00:18:32,454
Hello? Mum? Oh, what is it?
What's wrong, what have I done now?

237
00:18:32,540 --> 00:18:36,579
Ooh, this red top's falling to bits!
You should get your money back.

238
00:18:36,660 --> 00:18:41,734
Go on, there must be something.
You never phone in the middle
of the day... What's so funny?

239
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:45,654
Nothing. You all right, though?
Yeah, why wouldn't I be?

240
00:18:45,740 --> 00:18:49,972
What day is it? Wednesday all day.
You got a hangover?

241
00:18:50,060 --> 00:18:56,374
Ooh, I tell you what, put a quid
in that lottery syndicate. I'll pay
you back later. Yeah, um, I...

242
00:18:56,460 --> 00:19:03,377
I was just calling cos... I might
be late home. Is there something
wrong? No, I'm fine.

243
00:19:03,460 --> 00:19:06,540
Top of the world!

244
00:19:08,540 --> 00:19:12,374
Think THAT'S amazing,
you wanna see the bill.

245
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:16,520
That was five billion years ago.

246
00:19:16,140 --> 00:19:17,732
So...

247
00:19:17,820 --> 00:19:19,253
She's dead now.

248
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:24,450
Five billion years later,
my mum's dead.

249
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:26,417
Bundle of laughs, you are.

250
00:19:26,500 --> 00:19:28,456
BIG RUMBLE

251
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:33,256
That's not supposed to happen.

252
00:19:33,340 --> 00:19:36,776
Well, what was it? I'm just
getting green lights at this end.

253
00:19:36,860 --> 00:19:43,493
Honoured guests may be reassured
that gravity pockets may cause
slight turbulence. Thanking you...

254
00:19:43,580 --> 00:19:46,299
The whole place shook! I felt it!

255
00:19:46,380 --> 00:19:52,120
I've hosted all sorts of events
on platforms 1, 3, 6 and 15 and
never felt the slightest tremor.

256
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:54,819
I warn you, if this lot decide
to sue...!

257
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:56,936
I'm gonna scan the infrastructure.

258
00:20:00,780 --> 00:20:03,772
CLICKS AND SQUEAKS
What's that?

259
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:08,650
Control, I don't want to worry you
but I'm picking up readings...

260
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:13,450
I have no idea! They're small.
The scan says they're metal...

261
00:20:13,540 --> 00:20:15,770
I don't know what they look like!

262
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:22,452
Although I imagine they might look
rather like that.

263
00:20:25,620 --> 00:20:28,214
You're not on the guest list.

264
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:31,980
How did you get on board?

265
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:36,250
No! 'Sunfilter deactivated.'

266
00:20:36,340 --> 00:20:37,693
No!

267
00:20:37,780 --> 00:20:39,816
'Sunfilter descending.' No!

268
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:41,490
Sunfilter up!

269
00:20:41,140 --> 00:20:42,971
No, no, no!

270
00:20:43,060 --> 00:20:45,813
Control! Respond!
'Sunfilter descending.'

271
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:47,413
SUNFILTER UP!

272
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:50,617
'Sunfilter descending... '
HE SCREAMS

273
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:13,550
Indubitably, this is the Bad-Boo
scenario. I find the inherent laxity
of the unknown multiverse...

274
00:21:13,140 --> 00:21:19,900
That wasn't a gravity pocket, I know
gravity pockets, and they don't feel
like that... What d'you think, Jabe?

275
00:21:19,180 --> 00:21:22,934
Listen to the engines.
They've pitched up about 30 hertz.
Is that dodgy or what?!

276
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:29,289
It's the sound of metal - it doesn't
make any sense to me. Where's
the engine room? I don't know.

277
00:21:29,380 --> 00:21:35,250
But the maintenance duct
is just behind our guest suite.
I could show you. And... your wife.

278
00:21:35,340 --> 00:21:37,920
Oh, she's not my wife.

279
00:21:37,180 --> 00:21:39,455
Partner? No. Concubine?

280
00:21:39,540 --> 00:21:40,939
Nope.

281
00:21:41,020 --> 00:21:46,480
Prostitute? Whatever I am,
it must be invisible(!) D'you mind?!

282
00:21:46,140 --> 00:21:52,534
Tell you what, you two go...
pollinate. I'll catch up with family.
Quick word with Michael Jackson.

283
00:21:52,620 --> 00:21:54,417
Don't start a fight.

284
00:21:54,500 --> 00:21:56,968
I'm all yours.

285
00:21:58,700 --> 00:22:00,691
And I want you home by midnight.

286
00:22:00,780 --> 00:22:05,456
'Earth-death in 15 minutes.
Earth-death in 15 minutes.'

287
00:22:16,100 --> 00:22:20,930
Who's in charge of Platform One?
Has it got a captain or what?

288
00:22:20,180 --> 00:22:26,130
There's just the steward and staff.
All the rest is controlled by the
metalmind. You mean the computer?

289
00:22:26,220 --> 00:22:28,780
Well, who controls that?
The Corporation.

290
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:32,933
They move Platform One
from one artistic event to another.

291
00:22:33,020 --> 00:22:38,970
There's no-one from the corporation
on board? They're not needed.
This facility is purely automatic.

292
00:22:39,060 --> 00:22:40,812
It's the height of the Alpha Class.

293
00:22:40,900 --> 00:22:43,130
Nothing can go wrong. Unsinkable(?)

294
00:22:43,220 --> 00:22:46,769
If you like. The nautical metaphor
is appropriate.

295
00:22:46,860 --> 00:22:50,216
You're telling me! I was on board
another ship they called unsinkable.

296
00:22:50,300 --> 00:22:53,337
I ended up clinging to an iceberg.
Wasn't half cold.

297
00:22:53,420 --> 00:22:58,448
So what you're saying is
if we get in trouble,
there's no-one to help us out.

298
00:22:58,540 --> 00:23:01,213
I'm afraid not. Fantastic!

299
00:23:01,300 --> 00:23:02,938
I don't understand.

300
00:23:03,020 --> 00:23:05,818
In what way is that fantastic?

301
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:14,978
Soon the sun
will blossom into a red giant

302
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:16,573
And my home will die.

303
00:23:16,660 --> 00:23:20,130
That's where I used to live,
when I was a little boy. Down there.

304
00:23:20,220 --> 00:23:27,410
Mummy and Daddy had a house built
into the side of the Los Angeles
Crevasse. Ah, I'd have such fun.

305
00:23:27,500 --> 00:23:31,254
What happened to everyone else?
The human race, where did it go?

306
00:23:31,340 --> 00:23:35,458
They say mankind has touched
every star in the sky.

307
00:23:35,540 --> 00:23:37,531
So you're not the last human.

308
00:23:37,620 --> 00:23:41,135
I am the Last Pure Human.

309
00:23:41,220 --> 00:23:44,178
The others... mingled.

310
00:23:44,260 --> 00:23:49,209
Oh, they call themselves
New Humans and Protohumans and
Digihumans - even Human-ish -

311
00:23:49,300 --> 00:23:51,860
but d'you know what I call them?

312
00:23:51,940 --> 00:23:53,658
Mongrels.

313
00:23:53,740 --> 00:23:56,413
Right(!) And you stayed behind.

314
00:23:56,500 --> 00:23:59,378
I kept myself pure.

315
00:23:59,460 --> 00:24:01,815
How many operations have you had?

316
00:24:01,900 --> 00:24:04,500
708. Next week, it's 709.

317
00:24:04,140 --> 00:24:07,980
I'm having my blood bleached.

318
00:24:07,180 --> 00:24:10,172
Is that why you wanted a word?

319
00:24:10,260 --> 00:24:15,653
You could be flatter, Rose.
You've got a little bit
of a... chin poking out.

320
00:24:15,740 --> 00:24:18,937
I'd rather die.
Honestly, it doesn't hurt.

321
00:24:19,020 --> 00:24:21,170
I mean it. I would rather die.

322
00:24:21,260 --> 00:24:25,412
It's better to die than to live
like you, a bitchy trampoline.

323
00:24:25,500 --> 00:24:28,173
Oh, well, what do YOU know?

324
00:24:28,260 --> 00:24:30,854
I was born on that planet.

325
00:24:30,940 --> 00:24:36,173
And so was my mum, and so was my dad,
and that makes me, officially,
the last human being in this room.

326
00:24:36,260 --> 00:24:42,369
Cos you're not human. You've had it
all nipped and tucked and flattened
till there's nothing left.

327
00:24:42,460 --> 00:24:47,659
Anything human got chucked
in the bin. You're just skin,
Cassandra, lipstick and skin.

328
00:24:47,740 --> 00:24:49,219
Nice talking.

329
00:24:57,020 --> 00:25:01,650
So, tell me, Jabe,
what's a tree like you
doing in a place like this?

330
00:25:01,740 --> 00:25:06,256
Respect for the Earth.
Oh, come on, everyone on
this Platform's worth zillions.

331
00:25:06,340 --> 00:25:10,572
Well. Perhaps it's a case of having
to be seen at the right occasions.

332
00:25:10,660 --> 00:25:16,132
In case your share prices drop?
I know you lot, you've got massive
forests, roots everywhere.

333
00:25:16,220 --> 00:25:22,136
And there's always money in land.
All the same, we respect the Earth
as family.

334
00:25:22,220 --> 00:25:26,452
So many species evolved from
that planet. Mankind is only one.

335
00:25:26,540 --> 00:25:32,920
I'm another. My ancestors were
transplanted from the planet down
below, and I'm a direct descendant

336
00:25:32,180 --> 00:25:34,570
of the tropical rainforest.

337
00:25:34,140 --> 00:25:35,573
Excuse me.

338
00:25:37,860 --> 00:25:40,977
And what about your ancestry,
Doctor?

339
00:25:42,500 --> 00:25:46,288
Perhaps you could tell
a story or two.

340
00:25:46,380 --> 00:25:51,659
Perhaps a man only enjoys trouble
when there's nothing else left...?

341
00:25:53,340 --> 00:25:55,331
I scanned you earlier.

342
00:25:55,420 --> 00:25:59,379
The metalmachine had trouble
identifying your species.

343
00:25:59,460 --> 00:26:01,735
It refused to admit your existence.

344
00:26:01,820 --> 00:26:05,210
And even when it named you,
I wouldn't believe it.

345
00:26:05,300 --> 00:26:08,178
But it was right.

346
00:26:08,260 --> 00:26:10,569
I know where you're from!

347
00:26:12,140 --> 00:26:17,931
Forgive me for intruding, but
it's remarkable that you even exist.

348
00:26:18,020 --> 00:26:19,976
I just want to say...

349
00:26:21,020 --> 00:26:22,931
how sorry I am.

350
00:26:40,860 --> 00:26:43,420
SLOW CHUFFING

351
00:26:53,060 --> 00:26:56,291
Is it me, or is it a bit nippy?

352
00:27:10,220 --> 00:27:12,290
SHE CRIES OUT

353
00:27:17,780 --> 00:27:22,456
Fair do's though - that's a great
bit of air-conditioning. Sort of
nice and old-fashioned.

354
00:27:22,540 --> 00:27:24,576
Bet they call it retro.

355
00:27:25,660 --> 00:27:27,130
Gotcha.

356
00:27:32,060 --> 00:27:36,292
What the hell's that?
Is it part of the "retro"?

357
00:27:36,380 --> 00:27:38,496
I don't think so, hold on.

358
00:27:45,620 --> 00:27:48,259
Hey, nice liana. Thank you.

359
00:27:48,340 --> 00:27:50,331
Not supposed to show them in public.

360
00:27:50,420 --> 00:27:52,411
Don't worry, I won't tell anybody.

361
00:27:52,500 --> 00:27:56,493
Now then, who's been bringing their
pets on board? What does it do?

362
00:27:56,580 --> 00:27:59,697
Sabotage...
'Earth-death in ten minutes... '

363
00:27:59,780 --> 00:28:04,456
And the temperature's
about to rocket. Come on.
'... Earth death in ten minutes.'

364
00:28:04,540 --> 00:28:06,496
The planet's end!

365
00:28:06,580 --> 00:28:08,969
Come gather, come gather!

366
00:28:09,060 --> 00:28:12,939
Bid farewell to the cradle
of civilisation.

367
00:28:13,020 --> 00:28:16,410
Let us mourn her
with a traditional ballad.

368
00:28:19,420 --> 00:28:22,890
INTRO TO: "Toxic"
sung by Britney Spears

369
00:28:22,980 --> 00:28:26,814
# Baby, can't you see
I'm calling

370
00:28:26,900 --> 00:28:29,858
# A guy like you
Should wear a warning

371
00:28:29,940 --> 00:28:33,910
# It's dangerous
I'm fallin'... #

372
00:28:33,180 --> 00:28:36,650
SQUEAKS AND TRILLS
All right, hold on, get back.

373
00:28:36,740 --> 00:28:41,495
'Sunfilter rising.
Sunfilter rising.'

374
00:28:41,580 --> 00:28:44,811
Is the Steward in there?
You can smell him.

375
00:28:44,900 --> 00:28:49,576
Hold on. There's another sunfilter
programmed to descend.

376
00:28:49,660 --> 00:28:52,538
#... Too high
Can't come down

377
00:28:52,620 --> 00:28:54,190
# Losing my head
Spinning round and round

378
00:28:58,220 --> 00:29:00,780
# Do you feel me now...? #

379
00:29:00,860 --> 00:29:05,217
'Sunfilter descending.
Sunfilter descending... '

380
00:29:09,260 --> 00:29:12,580
'Sunfilter descending... '

381
00:29:12,140 --> 00:29:16,990
Let me out! Let me out!
'... Sunfilter descending... '

382
00:29:16,180 --> 00:29:18,570
LOUD BANGING

383
00:29:18,140 --> 00:29:20,449
Let me out! Let me out!

384
00:29:20,540 --> 00:29:24,692
'... Sunfilter descending.
Sunfilter descending... '

385
00:29:24,780 --> 00:29:26,418
MORE BANGING
Anyone in there?

386
00:29:26,500 --> 00:29:31,415
Let me out! Oh, well,
it would be you(!) Open the door!

387
00:29:31,500 --> 00:29:32,853
Give us two ticks...

388
00:29:32,940 --> 00:29:36,899
'... Sunfilter descending.
Sunfilter descending... '

389
00:29:39,220 --> 00:29:41,131
'Sunfilter rising. Sunfilter rising.

390
00:29:41,220 --> 00:29:43,290
'Sunfilter rising.
Sunfilter rising... '

391
00:29:45,140 --> 00:29:49,338
'... Sunfilter rising.
Sunfilter rising... '

392
00:29:49,420 --> 00:29:54,369
'Sunfilter descending... '
Just what we need -
the computer's getting clever.

393
00:29:54,460 --> 00:29:58,339
Stop mucking about! I'm not mucking
about! It's fighting back.

394
00:29:58,420 --> 00:30:01,537
'... Sunfilter descending... '
Open the door! I know!

395
00:30:01,620 --> 00:30:05,499
'... Sunfilter descending... '
The lock's melted!

396
00:30:05,580 --> 00:30:10,210
'... Sunfilter descending.
Sunfilter descending.

397
00:30:14,420 --> 00:30:19,289
'Sunfilter rising.
Sunfilter rising... '

398
00:30:24,140 --> 00:30:28,133
The whole thing's
jammed. I can't open the door.
Stay there, don't move.

399
00:30:28,220 --> 00:30:29,858
Where am I gonna go - Ipswich(?)

400
00:30:29,940 --> 00:30:31,931
'Earth-death in five minutes.'

401
00:30:34,460 --> 00:30:40,296
The metalmachine confirms.
The spider devices have infiltrated
the whole of Platform One.

402
00:30:40,380 --> 00:30:44,214
How's that possible? Our private
rooms are protected by a codewall.

403
00:30:44,300 --> 00:30:46,370
(Moisturise me, moisturise me!)

404
00:30:46,460 --> 00:30:50,419
Summon the Steward! I'm afraid the
Steward is dead.

405
00:30:50,500 --> 00:30:53,940
THEY GASP AND MURMUR

406
00:30:54,340 --> 00:30:56,137
Who killed him?

407
00:30:56,220 --> 00:31:00,896
This whole event was sponsored
by the Face of Boe. He invited us.
Talk to the Face, talk to the Face!

408
00:31:00,980 --> 00:31:04,734
Easy way of finding out. Someone
brought their little pet on board.

409
00:31:04,820 --> 00:31:06,458
Let's send him back to master.

410
00:31:27,260 --> 00:31:31,940
The Adherents of the Repeated Meme!
J'accuse!

411
00:31:31,180 --> 00:31:36,493
That's all very well,
and really kind of obvious but,
if you stop and think about it...

412
00:31:37,180 --> 00:31:39,648
A repeated meme is just an idea.

413
00:31:39,740 --> 00:31:42,732
And that's all they are, an idea.

414
00:31:45,860 --> 00:31:49,819
Remote-control 'droids. Nice little
cover for the real troublemaker.

415
00:31:49,900 --> 00:31:52,334
Go on, Jimbo. Go home.

416
00:31:54,340 --> 00:31:56,251
GUESTS GASP

417
00:31:56,340 --> 00:31:59,377
I bet you were the school swot
and never got kissed.

418
00:31:59,460 --> 00:32:00,779
At arms!

419
00:32:00,860 --> 00:32:02,498
What you gonna do, moisturise me?

420
00:32:02,580 --> 00:32:04,130
With acid.

421
00:32:04,100 --> 00:32:08,252
Oh, you're too late, anyway.
My spiders have control
of the mainframe.

422
00:32:08,340 --> 00:32:13,619
Oh, you all carried them as gifts,
tax-free, past every codewall.

423
00:32:13,700 --> 00:32:19,218
I'm not just a pretty face.
Sabotaging a ship while you're
inside it, how stupid's that?

424
00:32:19,300 --> 00:32:22,337
I'd hoped to manufacture
a hostage situation.

425
00:32:22,420 --> 00:32:27,500
With myself as one of the victims,
the compensation
would have been enormous.

426
00:32:27,140 --> 00:32:30,610
Five billion years,
and it still comes down to money.

427
00:32:30,700 --> 00:32:33,533
D'you think it's cheap,
looking like this?

428
00:32:33,620 --> 00:32:36,418
Flatness costs a fortune!

429
00:32:36,500 --> 00:32:38,809
I am the Last Human, Doctor.

430
00:32:38,900 --> 00:32:43,576
Me, not that freaky little kid
of yours.

431
00:32:43,660 --> 00:32:45,855
Arrest her! The infidel!

432
00:32:45,940 --> 00:32:50,218
Oh, shut it, pixie!
I've still got my final option.

433
00:32:50,300 --> 00:32:52,530
'Earth-death in three minutes,
Earth-death in three minutes... '

434
00:32:52,620 --> 00:32:56,408
And here it comes. You're
just as useful dead, all of you.

435
00:32:56,500 --> 00:33:01,449
I have shares in
your rival companies. They'll triple
in price as soon as you're dead.

436
00:33:01,540 --> 00:33:05,533
My spiders are primed and ready
to destroy the safety systems.

437
00:33:05,620 --> 00:33:07,850
How did that old Earth song go?

438
00:33:07,940 --> 00:33:09,578
"Burn baby, burn."

439
00:33:09,660 --> 00:33:11,457
Then you'll burn with us!

440
00:33:11,540 --> 00:33:13,656
Oh, I'm so sorry!

441
00:33:13,740 --> 00:33:18,495
I know the use of teleportation is
strictly forbidden, but...

442
00:33:18,580 --> 00:33:20,377
I'm such a naughty thing.

443
00:33:20,460 --> 00:33:20,733
Spiders, activate!

444
00:33:21,140 --> 00:33:23,370
Spiders, activate!

445
00:33:23,460 --> 00:33:26,816
THUNDEROUS WHOOSHES

446
00:33:31,820 --> 00:33:35,699
Force-fields gone,
with the planet about to explode...

447
00:33:35,780 --> 00:33:37,850
At least it'll be quick.

448
00:33:37,940 --> 00:33:44,334
Just like my fifth husband... Oops!
Oh, shame on me! Bye bye, darlings.

449
00:33:44,420 --> 00:33:46,980
'Safety systems failing... '
Bye-bye, my darlings!

450
00:33:47,060 --> 00:33:49,972
'... Heat levels rising... '

451
00:33:50,060 --> 00:33:52,733
Reset the computer!
Only the Steward would know how.

452
00:33:52,820 --> 00:33:57,257
No, we can do it by hand.
There must be a "system restore"
switch. Jabe, come on.

453
00:33:57,340 --> 00:33:59,296
You lot, just chill.

454
00:33:59,380 --> 00:34:00,449
'... Heat levels rising... '

455
00:34:04,500 --> 00:34:08,618
'Earthdeath in two minutes.
Earthdeath in two minutes.'

456
00:34:10,300 --> 00:34:15,215
'Heat levels critical,
heat levels critical.'

457
00:34:19,140 --> 00:34:21,176
'... Heat levels rising.
Heat levels rising.'

458
00:34:21,420 --> 00:34:21,932
Oh, and guess where the switch is(!)

459
00:34:22,020 --> 00:34:26,411
'... Heat levels rising.
Heat levels rising.'

460
00:34:36,140 --> 00:34:40,190
External temperature
5, 000 degrees.

461
00:34:48,180 --> 00:34:53,334
You can't, the heat's gonna vent
through this place. I know. Jabe!

462
00:34:53,420 --> 00:34:57,538
You're made of wood. Then stop
wasting time - Time Lord.

463
00:35:00,500 --> 00:35:02,491
'Heat levels rising...

464
00:35:02,580 --> 00:35:04,491
'Heat levels rising.'

465
00:35:04,580 --> 00:35:08,539
'... Heat levels hazardous... '

466
00:35:08,620 --> 00:35:12,533
We're going to die!
'... Heat levels hazardous... '

467
00:35:25,660 --> 00:35:27,571
'Shields malfunction...

468
00:35:29,740 --> 00:35:32,812
'Shields malfunction.

469
00:35:32,900 --> 00:35:36,970
'Shields malfunction.
Shields malfunction.

470
00:35:36,180 --> 00:35:39,252
'Shields malfunction... '

471
00:35:43,860 --> 00:35:49,969
'Heat levels critical...
Heat levels critical.'

472
00:36:01,660 --> 00:36:07,610
'Heat levels rising.
Heat levels rising.'

473
00:36:07,700 --> 00:36:09,930
JABE SCREAMS

474
00:36:10,940 --> 00:36:13,249
SCREAMS STOP

475
00:36:33,340 --> 00:36:35,854
'Planet explodes in...

476
00:36:35,940 --> 00:36:38,374
'... ten,

477
00:36:38,460 --> 00:36:40,894
nine...

478
00:36:40,980 --> 00:36:43,448
eight...

479
00:36:44,700 --> 00:36:47,134
..seven...

480
00:36:48,700 --> 00:36:50,990
..six...

481
00:36:51,900 --> 00:36:53,253
..five...

482
00:36:53,340 --> 00:36:56,457
fou... four...

483
00:36:59,580 --> 00:37:01,536
Raise shields!

484
00:37:01,620 --> 00:37:02,848
..one.

485
00:37:18,420 --> 00:37:23,574
'Exoglass repair.
Exoglass repair... '

486
00:37:26,620 --> 00:37:29,214
'Exoglass repair.
Exoglass repair... '

487
00:38:07,700 --> 00:38:10,890
HE MURMURS

488
00:38:16,100 --> 00:38:18,216
You all right? Yeah, I'm fine.

489
00:38:18,300 --> 00:38:20,575
I'm full of ideas.
I'm bristling with 'em!

490
00:38:20,660 --> 00:38:25,973
Idea number one.
Teleportation through 5, 000 degrees
needs some kind of feed.

491
00:38:26,060 --> 00:38:30,338
Idea number two.
This feed must be hidden nearby.

492
00:38:32,660 --> 00:38:34,651
Idea number three.

493
00:38:34,740 --> 00:38:39,520
If you're as clever as me, then a
teleportation-feed can be reversed.

494
00:38:40,100 --> 00:38:44,332
..Oh, you should've seen
their little alien faces...

495
00:38:45,820 --> 00:38:47,173
Oh.

496
00:38:47,260 --> 00:38:49,410
The last human. So.

497
00:38:49,500 --> 00:38:51,411
You passed my little test. Bravo!

498
00:38:51,500 --> 00:38:54,537
This makes you eligible to join, um,
the... the Human Club.

499
00:38:54,620 --> 00:38:59,648
People have died, Cassandra.
You murdered them. It depends
on your definition of people.

500
00:38:59,740 --> 00:39:03,653
And that's enough of a technicality
to keep your lawyers dizzy
for centuries.

501
00:39:03,740 --> 00:39:06,891
Take me to court then, Doctor,

502
00:39:06,980 --> 00:39:09,778
and watch me smile and cry...
QUIET CREAKS

503
00:39:09,860 --> 00:39:11,816
..and flutter. And creak?

504
00:39:11,900 --> 00:39:15,415
And what? Creak. You're creaking.

505
00:39:15,500 --> 00:39:16,899
What?

506
00:39:17,260 --> 00:39:19,899
Agh! I-I'm drying out!

507
00:39:19,980 --> 00:39:23,655
Oh, sweet heavens!
Moisturise me, moisturise me!

508
00:39:23,740 --> 00:39:29,497
Where are my surgeons,
my lovely boys? It's too hot!
YOU raised the temperature.

509
00:39:29,580 --> 00:39:31,930
Have pity!

510
00:39:31,180 --> 00:39:33,375
SHE GROWLS:
Moisturise me!

511
00:39:33,460 --> 00:39:35,416
Oh, Doctor!

512
00:39:35,500 --> 00:39:40,369
Oh, Doctor, I'll do anything...!
Help her. Everything has its time.
And everything dies.

513
00:39:40,460 --> 00:39:44,900
I'm... too... young...!

514
00:39:57,260 --> 00:39:59,820
'Shuttles four and six departing.

515
00:39:59,900 --> 00:40:03,529
'This unit now closing
down for maintenance.'

516
00:40:18,180 --> 00:40:20,455
The end of the Earth.

517
00:40:21,460 --> 00:40:23,980
It's gone.

518
00:40:26,220 --> 00:40:29,769
We were too busy saving ourselves.
No-one saw it go.

519
00:40:33,660 --> 00:40:38,131
All those years, all that history,
and no-one was even looking.

520
00:40:39,540 --> 00:40:41,190
It's just...

521
00:40:42,900 --> 00:40:44,413
Come with me.

522
00:41:11,660 --> 00:41:13,730
A TODDLER CRIES

523
00:41:25,740 --> 00:41:27,731
Big Issue!

524
00:41:29,060 --> 00:41:30,971
Big Issue...!

525
00:41:31,060 --> 00:41:35,611
You think it'll last forever,
people and cars and concrete.

526
00:41:35,700 --> 00:41:37,656
But it won't.

527
00:41:37,740 --> 00:41:40,129
One day, it's all gone.

528
00:41:40,220 --> 00:41:42,654
Even the sky.

529
00:41:48,540 --> 00:41:50,815
My planet's gone.

530
00:41:51,820 --> 00:41:53,697
It's dead.

531
00:41:55,420 --> 00:41:58,590
It burned, like the Earth.

532
00:41:58,140 --> 00:42:00,893
It's just rocks and dust.

533
00:42:01,860 --> 00:42:03,771
Before its time.

534
00:42:04,820 --> 00:42:06,856
What happened?

535
00:42:08,420 --> 00:42:11,173
There was a war, and we lost.

536
00:42:11,260 --> 00:42:12,739
A war with who?

537
00:42:16,620 --> 00:42:18,611
What about your people?

538
00:42:19,740 --> 00:42:21,890
I'm a Time Lord.

539
00:42:21,980 --> 00:42:24,858
I'm the last of the Time Lords.

540
00:42:24,940 --> 00:42:26,817
They're all gone.

541
00:42:26,900 --> 00:42:28,891
I'm the only survivor.

542
00:42:29,940 --> 00:42:32,818
I'm left travelling on my own
cos there's no-one else.

543
00:42:34,340 --> 00:42:35,898
There's me.

544
00:42:39,020 --> 00:42:42,490
You've seen how dangerous it is.
D'you wanna go home?

545
00:42:45,860 --> 00:42:47,373
I don't know.

546
00:42:49,020 --> 00:42:51,900
I want...

547
00:42:53,980 --> 00:42:56,289
Can you smell chips?

548
00:42:56,380 --> 00:42:58,132
Yeah.

549
00:42:58,220 --> 00:43:00,495
Yeah! I want chips.

550
00:43:00,580 --> 00:43:06,974
Me too. Right, then. Before
you get me back in that box, chips
it is. And you can pay. No money.

551
00:43:07,060 --> 00:43:10,689
What sort of date are you? Come on,
then, tightwad. Chips are on me.

552
00:43:10,780 --> 00:43:14,659
We've only got five billion years
till the shops close.

553
00:43:24,180 --> 00:43:27,297
Now - you've seen the future,
so let's have a look at the past.

554
00:43:27,380 --> 00:43:32,408
1860, how does 1860 sound?
What happened in 1860?
I don't know. Let's find out.

555
00:43:32,500 --> 00:43:38,894
..I can't believe she's gone.
Not gone, Mr Redpath, sir.
Merely sleeping.

556
00:43:39,900 --> 00:43:45,258
She's up and on her feet and out
there somewhere. Mr Sneed for shame,
how many more times? It's ungodly!

557
00:43:45,340 --> 00:43:48,377
'... Excuse me, sir.
Mr Dickens, this is your call.'

558
00:43:48,460 --> 00:43:53,900
..Use the sight. Find the old lady
or you're dismissed.

559
00:43:53,180 --> 00:43:55,614
What phantasmagoria is this?

560
00:43:57,980 --> 00:43:59,413
That's more like it!
